  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide Lifesaving Multi Sectoral Assistance to South Sudan Returnees Affected by Sudan Crisis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sudan crisis has significantly impacted the humanitarian situation in South Sudan, leading to the displacement of more than 98,692 individuals crossing the Sudan-South Sudan border as per Joint IOM-UNHCR-RRC flow monitoring dashboard. Through this project, IOM seeks to identify the most vulnerable new arrivals at prioritized points of entry (PoE) and provide lifesaving multi-sectoral and tailored support to the most vulnerable South Sudan returnees in Upper Nile, Unity, and Greater Bahr el Ghazal.</narrative>
  </description>
